From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: dwc3-am62: fix spurious wake immediately after
 suspend in host mode

dwc3_ti_suspend_common() unconditionally armed USBSS_WAKEUP_CFG_LINESTATE_EN
whenever the port was in host mode. LINESTATE reflects the raw D+/D- line
state, and nothing in this glue driver verifies the link has actually
settled into U2/L3 (suspended) before that bit is armed -- the accompanying
comment even says as much ("causes spurious wake-up"), but it was attached
to the wrong branch and never enforced. In practice this fires the moment
WAKEUP_CONFIG is written, waking the system right back up on entry to
suspend whenever the port is in host mode.

AM62 also has no overcurrent-sense pin routed for this port, so
USBSS_WAKEUP_CFG_OVERCURRENT_EN is a harmless no-op here, but it's kept so
host mode still has a (currently unused) wakeup source instead of none, in
case a future board revision wires it up.

Since LINESTATE can't be safely gated from this glue, drop it from the
host-mode wakeup config entirely. Also log USBSS_WAKEUP_STAT on resume so
the responsible bit is visible in dmesg if a spurious wake reappears.

Signed-off-by: Boris Krasnovskiy <boris.krasnovskiy@ezurio.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-am62.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-am62.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-am62.c
@@ -337,7 +337,7 @@ static int dwc3_ti_suspend_common(struct
 		/* Set wakeup config enable bits */
 		reg = dwc3_ti_readl(am62, USBSS_WAKEUP_CONFIG);
 		if (current_prtcap_dir == DWC3_GCTL_PRTCAP_HOST) {
-			reg = USBSS_WAKEUP_CFG_LINESTATE_EN | USBSS_WAKEUP_CFG_OVERCURRENT_EN;
+			reg = USBSS_WAKEUP_CFG_OVERCURRENT_EN;
 		} else {
 			reg = USBSS_WAKEUP_CFG_VBUSVALID_EN | USBSS_WAKEUP_CFG_SESSVALID_EN;
 			/*
@@ -380,6 +380,13 @@ static int dwc3_ti_resume_common(struct
 	reg = dwc3_ti_readl(am62, USBSS_WAKEUP_STAT);
 	am62->wakeup_stat = reg;
 
+	if (reg)
+		dev_info(dev, "wakeup_stat: 0x%x%s%s%s%s\n", reg,
+			reg & USBSS_WAKEUP_STAT_OVERCURRENT ? " OVERCURRENT" : "",
+			reg & USBSS_WAKEUP_STAT_LINESTATE ? " LINESTATE" : "",
+			reg & USBSS_WAKEUP_STAT_SESSVALID ? " SESSVALID" : "",
+			reg & USBSS_WAKEUP_STAT_VBUSVALID ? " VBUSVALID" : "");
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
